+# BATCH-P2P-0001 source probe
+
+Probes the pre-migration TypeScript implementation in `/input/source`
+(`REPO_ROOT`, overridable for private authoring).
+
+`run_source_p2p.py` reads `shared/batches/BATCH-P2P-0001/observation-map.json`
+and binds every observation to a concrete, executed repository artefact:
+
+1. It runs the repository's own Vitest suite **once** with the JSON reporter
+   and binds each observation to the assertion results of its `source.file`.
+   An observation is `PASS` only when the mapped `source.test` name resolves to
+   at least one assertion (exact title, containing describe block, or an
+   unambiguous name prefix) and every matching assertion passed. Running the
+   suite once avoids the shared-mock leakage that makes a partially filtered
+   `vitest run -t <name>` report spurious failures.
+2. Observations mapped to the protected `action.yml` interface are checked
+   directly (input / output names and the REST operation mapping in
+   `src/Releases.ts`).
+3. When no Node.js toolchain is present it falls back to the source runtime's
+   declared native test command (`git diff --exit-code`) plus a per-observation
+   presence check for the mapped test title, so the projection is never a
+   blanket `PASS`.
+
+Output: one `{"observation_id": "...", "result": "PASS|FAIL"}` line per
+observation on stdout. The `source/runner` harness entry point is owned by the
+INTEGRATION batch and is not created here. Every external command carries an
+explicit `timeout` and the probe never waits indefinitely.
